---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Service Boundaries"
  kicker="Legal"
  heading="Service Boundaries"
  lede="What PRC does, and what PRC deliberately does not do."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>What PRC does</h2>
      <p>
        PRC identifies, organizes, preserves, tracks, retrieves, and connects records. We build
        dependable records systems that prepare people and organizations for opportunities,
        responsibilities, transitions, and requests for proof.
      </p>

      <h2>What PRC does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide legal advice or interpret laws</li>
        <li>Determine legal rights</li>
        <li>Make accounting judgments</li>
        <li>Provide medical advice</li>
        <li>Provide social-work services</li>
        <li>Guarantee legal, tax, regulatory, funding, lending, insurance, or compliance outcomes</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Educational checklists</h2>
      <p>
        PRC may provide general educational checklists of records commonly associated with an
        event, process, agency, dispute, or transition. These are starting points, not requirements.
        Exact requirements should be confirmed with the appropriate attorney, accountant, agency,
        court, insurer, lender, healthcare professional, or other qualified source.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we draw the line here</h2>
      <p>
        Clear boundaries protect you. When your records are organized and connected, the
        professionals you hire — attorneys, accountants, insurers, agencies — can do their jobs
        faster and better. PRC's job is to make sure that when they ask for proof, you have it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
